                <pb facs="0264" n="214" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg214"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Subinclosure.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Copy article 7 of the concession of the railroad from
                        Samana Bay to La Veza.</hi></head>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Art</hi>. 7. The railroad and all its accessories in
                    movable and immovable property, as well as its capital and the rent produced,
                    shall enjoy exemption from all kinds of imposts and fiscal and municipal
                    contributions during fifteen years only, and also the vessels in which are
                    imported only the materials necessary for the construction and reparation of the
                    railroad shall be exempted from the port charges and the said materials from
                    custom duties.</p>
                <p>This franchise shall not be enjoyed by the products of the soil in regard to
                    export duties nor by the vessels in which the export is made.</p>
                <p>Concession May 5, 1893.</p>
                <p>(Collection of laws, <ref target="#pg276">p. 276</ref>, No. 8.)</p>
            </div>
